# Titan Orbit — headless server rebuild guidance

The deployed authoritative game runs as a **Unity Dedicated Server** build (`UNITY_SERVER`, IL2CPP). Editor Play Mode / MPPM can validate server logic without a full player build, but **GCE and any external headless binary only pick up changes after a rebuild + redeploy**.

After completing any task that touches project files, **always end the response with a `## Headless server rebuild` section** (even for small or docs-only changes). Use one of: **Required**, **Not required**, or **Uncertain — verify in Editor first**.

---

## Build commands (when Required)

| Target | Unity menu | Output folder |
|--------|------------|---------------|
| GCE / Linux (primary) | **TitanOrbit → Build → Headless Server (Linux — Google Cloud)** | `BuildOutput/Server/TitanOrbitLinux1` |
| Local Windows headless | **TitanOrbit → Build → Headless Server (Windows)** | `BuildOutput/Server/headless-windows` |

After Linux build: deploy with `tools/gce/` (e.g. `upload_linux_build_to_gce.bat` or GCS pipeline). **Quit the Unity Editor before packing/upload** so IL2CPP artifacts are not truncated.

---

## Required — rebuild and redeploy

Changes that affect **authoritative server runtime** (anything compiled into or baked for the dedicated server):

- **ECS server systems** — `[WorldSystemFilter(...ServerSimulation)]`, or systems that run on the server world only.
- **Shared simulation** — `ShipMovementLogic`, `ShipMotorSimulator`, `BulletSimulationSystem`, combat/economy/orbit logic, physics bootstrap, anything both client prediction and server authority call.
- **NetCode / networking** — ghost components and fields, RPC commands (`IRpcCommand`), RPC handlers, `TitanOrbitSessionManager`, dedicated boot (`TitanOrbitBootstrap`, relay/lobby), tick rate, connection/driver code.
- **ECS components & data** — new/changed `IComponentData`, ghost-serialized fields, buffers, enableable flags used in sim or RPCs.
- **Authoring & baking** — `*GhostAuthoring.cs`, bakers, SubScenes, prefab components that bake entities (colliders, ghost types, physics layers in `TitanOrbitPhysicsLayers`).
- **Scenes & startup** — `EditorBuildSettings` enabled scenes, bootstrap scenes, server auto-boot markers.
- **Server `#if UNITY_SERVER` paths** — any logic under `UNITY_SERVER` (not stripped in dedicated builds).
- **Gameplay prefabs/assets referenced at bake or server startup** — ship/planet/asteroid ghosts, spawn configs, ScriptableObjects read by server systems.

When in doubt: if it can change **what the server simulates, serializes, or validates**, treat as **Required**.

---

## Not required — no headless rebuild

Safe to skip dedicated server build/redeploy:

- **Editor-only** — `Assets/Editor/`, `*.Editor.asmdef`, `#if UNITY_EDITOR`-only code, Cursor rules, docs, CI/deploy scripts under `tools/` that do not change game C#.
- **Pure client presentation** — visual proxies (`EcsWorldVisualizer`, `ShipVisualSyncSystem`, propulsion/bank VFX), camera/HUD/UI under `Assets/Scripts/UI/`, audio, minimap cosmetics, Shapes/VFX with no sim impact.
- **Client-only prediction wiring** — e.g. `ShipClientPredictedMovementSystem`, `ShipInputApplySystem`, **only if** shared motor/sim code was untouched.
- **Non-game repo churn** — `.gitignore`, layout files (`UserSettings/Layouts/`), performance test JSON, build logs, `.meta`-only.

Editor Play Mode / MPPM host still reload scripts automatically; say **Not required (Editor/MPPM sufficient for local server testing)** when that applies.

---

## Response template (mandatory)

Every agent reply that made or reviewed file changes must include:

```markdown
## Headless server rebuild
**Verdict:** Required | Not required | Uncertain — verify in Editor first
**Why:** One or two sentences tied to the files changed.
**If required:** TitanOrbit → Build → Headless Server (Linux — Google Cloud) → deploy via tools/gce/…
**If not required:** Optional note (e.g. test in Editor with Local host, or client/WebGL-only).
```

For multi-file changes, list the **highest-impact** path (server sim > NetCode > shared > client-only).

---

## Quick examples

| Change | Verdict |
|--------|---------|
| `ShipMovementLogic.cs`, `BulletSimulationSystem.cs` | **Required** — authoritative sim |
| `StarshipGhostAuthoring.cs`, ghost field on a component | **Required** — bake/serialization |
| `NetworkCommands.cs` or RPC handler system | **Required** — server validates RPCs |
| `EcsWorldVisualizer.cs`, `ShipSpeedometerHUD.cs` | **Not required** — presentation only |
| `TitanOrbitBuildAutomation.cs` (Editor) | **Not required** — build tooling only |
| `ShipClientPredictedMovementSystem.cs` only, no shared logic change | **Not required** for deploy; server uses `ShipMovementSystem` |
| Shader/material on ship mesh, no collider/ghost change | **Not required** — visual only |
